a.endpoint_correspondence={
E001:{mode:"equivalent",explanation:"EFlow encodes the complete source suite on normalized Fourier coefficients: all nonnegative orders, uniform homogeneous flow and Galerkin bounds, bounded-set Lipschitz dependence, uniqueness in the source L∞L² coefficient class, conservation, compatibility by uniqueness, smooth approximation, and the positive-order subsequence's strong L^q_t dot H^sigma and weak-* L∞_t dot H^s convergence. sourceB has exp(+i3kabt), SourceTwist u=S_t u, so its physical equation is U_t=UU_x+U_xxx. MemDot/DotCont are exactly the source mean-zero homogeneous completions and topology. Galerkin projects both inputs/output and freezes high coefficients. WeakStarDot tests all L¹ paths in the homogeneous Hilbert space via its weighted inner product, exactly its predual; StrongTime uses the qth-power integral for every real finite q>1. Fourier testing and reconstruction identify this with the source physical formulation in both directions; no numerical error estimate is assumed."},
E002:{mode:"equivalent",explanation:"For each B0 and theta∈(-1,0], C,D are positive and chosen before Q and the two data/solutions. DotUB gives the source bound C D^Q times the initial dot H^theta distance at every time; on the continuous solution paths this equals the time supremum. SourceTwist is the source common multiplier exp(+itk³), and the physical and twisted distances coincide coefficientwise, so retaining both inequalities is equivalent to the stated single source estimate plus its unitary reformulation. Data 0 means precisely real mean-zero normalized L²."},
E003:{mode:"equivalent",explanation:"ETri is Proposition 3.4 for all alpha∈[0,1], 0≤a≤b, b-a≤1 and weakly differentiable L∞H^alpha paths. XPath states exactly coordinate measurability, Sobolev membership and finite essential bounds, plus the weak time derivative. Countable Fourier coordinates characterize the corresponding Hilbert-valued measurable classes. srcN/srcX multiply each normalized norm by sqrt(2π); SrcTriBound quantifies all three negative-norm slots without changing the trilinear operator or constants' uniformity. The second clause retains the constant-input H^sigma bound for all sigma∈[0,1]. Coefficientwise convolution/integration agrees on the smooth core and hence on the bounded extension; conversely the Fourier representation reconstructs those same Sobolev/distribution classes."},
E004:{mode:"equivalent",explanation:"EStage retains 0<sigma≤1, any positive timestep, every natural grid index n, every t∈[nτ,nτ+τ], and all time-independent mean-zero H^sigma inputs. beta0 has exactly the three source cases and beta is restricted to [beta0,1+sigma]; the real power is (1+sigma-beta)/(1+sigma-beta0). The existence of epsilon0 followed by every epsilon∈(0,epsilon0) expresses 'any sufficiently small fixed positive epsilon'. C is chosen after sigma,epsilon,beta and before n,tau,t and inputs. srcN retains the unnormalized source norm, and stage includes the source factor 1/2. Fourier completion identifies the input/output spaces in both directions."},
E005:{mode:"equivalent",explanation:"EProduct retains the source range sigma∈[0,1], all four a(sigma) cases including both positive epsilon endpoints, the admissibility threshold, and the source factor sqrt(2π) in each norm. mul is the Fourier coefficient convolution of the product; on these Sobolev domains the asserted L² membership and bound identify exactly the source pointwise product by density. The same Fourier identification converts the inequality in both directions. Epsilon and the constant are chosen before f,g."},
E006:{mode:"direct",explanation:"Endpoint copies the exact twisted update for every tau>0, natural n and smooth real mean-zero f, with uold=S_(nτ)f. psi is the displayed four-term physical update, stage is the half B integral, Cst is the B(f,stage) integral, and rem is precisely -τ/(18ik) times the double frequency sum with alpha=3ab(a+b), beta=3kc(a+b), the covariance eta and exp(-it_n(alpha+beta)); output zero and a+b=0 are handled exactly as in D015. No cutoff, asymptotic error or convergence premise is introduced."},
P:{mode:"equivalent",explanation:"Universally closing the parameters T,gamma,R under H001-H003 gives exactly T>0,0<gamma≤1,R>0. Target chooses C>0,tau0>0 before every real mean-zero datum in the whole H^gamma ball and every positive integer L with tau=T/L≤tau0. Exact is the unique real mean-zero continuous H^gamma distributional KdV flow, encoded by its integrated twisted Fourier equation and uniform H^gamma smooth approximation. Fourier testing gives the physical PDE from this equation and conversely, since continuous L² paths give continuous convolution coefficients; smooth scalar Fourier-test approximation justifies the distributional reconstruction. GridError asserts each unfiltered recursive iterate is real mean-zero L² and gives the normalized L² error ≤C tau^gamma at every n≤L, equivalent to the maximum on the finite grid. Numerical uses exactly psi with no frequency filter. Weighted square-summable coefficients are the specified Sobolev completion, so the quantification covers all original rough data and conversely. Constants cannot depend on the datum, L, Fourier support or additional smoothness because all are quantified after C,tau0."}
};
